WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:03.650
Wealth, fame, power...

3
00:00:02.940 --> 00:00:04.440
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

4
00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.820
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates, obtained everything the world has to offer.

5
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:07.360
attained this and everything else
the world had to offer.

6
00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:10.820
And his dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

7
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.660
What he said in his final moments drove countless souls to the seas.

8
00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:13.660
You want my treasure?

9
00:00:12.370 --> 00:00:13.700
You can have it!

10
00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:15.450
Go ahead.

11
00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.040
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

12
00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:16.660
Find it!

13
00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:19.250
Everything is right where I left it!

14
00:00:17.040 --> 00:00:19.250
Now you just have to find it!

15
00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:23.750
These words lured
men to the Grand Line

16
00:00:21.670 --> 00:00:26.380
People set their sights on the Grand Line in pursuit of their dreams.

17
00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.920
in pursuit of dreams greater than
they'd ever dared to imagine!

18
00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:29.630
The world has truly entered the Great Pirate Era!

19
00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:29.850
This is the time known as
the Great Pirate Era!

20
00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:35.640
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

21
00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:41.440
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

22
00:00:41.770 --> 00:00:42.690
One Piece!

23
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.700
Compasses? Not for me. Left them all behind

24
00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:58.500
I'm headed out to sea, with my heart serving as guide

25
00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:04.540
Following the ancient map to the spot marked "X" reveals

26
00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:09.760
Yeah, it's only legendary till someone proves it's real

27
00:01:11.380 --> 00:01:13.710
When the world's got you down,

28
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:16.850
lean on your crew, they'll turn it around

29
00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.190
Their biorhythm will carry you through

30
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.230
We're gonna make the most of it

31
00:01:26.110 --> 00:01:31.400
Come aboard and bring along all your hopes and dreams

32
00:01:31.610 --> 00:01:36.990
I know together we'll find everything we're looking for

33
00:01:37.330 --> 00:01:40.040
Got some change to my name,

34
00:01:40.040 --> 00:01:43.250
and maybe you wanna be my friend?

35
00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:48.130
We are, we are on the cruise!

36
00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:49.760
WE ARE!

37
00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:53.680
<b>Enter: Sanji</b>

38
00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.720
[LUFFY] That was way off the mark!

39
00:01:59.720 --> 00:02:00.390
[ZORO grunts]

40
00:02:00.390 --> 00:02:02.350
Hey, what's so loud down there?

41
00:02:02.350 --> 00:02:06.360
Cannon firing practice!
But it's not going very well.

42
00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:10.030
Like I said... Let the
expert aim the thing.

43
00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:13.740
Judging from the flying distance
of the last one, this should do it.

44
00:02:13.740 --> 00:02:15.410
Fire!

45
00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:19.370
[LUFFY] Awesome! You hit
that thing on the first try!

46
00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:21.500
[USOPP] Wow, I did.

47
00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:23.540
Whatcha think? I'm pretty magnificent

48
00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.710
when it comes to aiming!
So, are you impressed yet?!

49
00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:27.460
Yeah! You better believe it!

50
00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.670
So it's all settled.
You'll be our sniper.

51
00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:31.550
[USOPP] Wait, I don't get to be captain?

52
00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:33.220
[LUFFY] No. I'm still the captain!

53
00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.680
– [ZORO chuckles]
– [USOPP laughs]

54
00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:37.890
[USOPP] Whatever. I'll
humor you for now, but...

55
00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.850
the second you do something
cowardly, I'm taking your post!

56
00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:43.940
I can live with that. But, you
know guys, I was thinking.

57
00:02:43.940 --> 00:02:46.400
There's one other position
that we have to fill

58
00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:48.360
before we can head out
for the Grand Line.

59
00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:51.030
You're right. The kitchen
is really nice on this ship.

60
00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.820
Just... pay me, and I'll do it.

61
00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:54.950
[ZORO] I suppose it
is vital for long trips.

62
00:02:54.950 --> 00:02:57.910
[LUFFY] No decent pirate ship
should be without one.

63
00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:59.330
A musician.

64
00:02:59.330 --> 00:03:00.660
[ZORO] Are you an idiot?

65
00:03:00.660 --> 00:03:02.660
[NAMI] What do you think
we're doing out here?!

66
00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:05.210
[USOPP] Just when I thought you
were gonna say something smart.

67
00:03:05.210 --> 00:03:06.370
[LUFFY] But we're pirates.

68
00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:10.250
And Pirates sing a lot!
Didn't you know?

69
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:12.260
[JOHNNY] Get out here ya damn pirates!

70
00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:13.090
[LUFFY] Hm?!

71
00:03:13.090 --> 00:03:14.170
[ZORO] Hm?

72
00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:17.550
Hey! What the hell? Who are you?

73
00:03:17.550 --> 00:03:20.260
[JOHNNY] Shut up!
Who I am means nothing!

74
00:03:20.260 --> 00:03:21.720
Ya stinkin' pirate!

75
00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.270
– [JOHNNY grunts]
– [LUFFY screams]

76
00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.390
Hey, guys, how many are there?

77
00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.560
Uh... One.

78
00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:31.110
Then just let him handle it.

79
00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:34.110
Over the years I've lost count
of all the pirate heads

80
00:03:31.110 --> 00:03:36.530
Tattoo: "Sea"

81
00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.530
we've taken. And now you guys think...

82
00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.370
you can kill my partner?! [grunts]

83
00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:41.030
[ZORO] Hm? That voice.

84
00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:42.700
[LUFFY] What do you mean by 'partner'?

85
00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.620
Look I don't know what this is...

86
00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.080
But just stop wrecking our ship!

87
00:03:47.080 --> 00:03:48.540
[JOHNNY screams]

88
00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:51.380
[JOHNNY gasping]

89
00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:53.340
[JOHNNY] Lost by a hair.

90
00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:54.340
Who is this guy?

91
00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:56.760
[JOHNNY groaning]

92
00:03:56.760 --> 00:04:00.600
[ZORO] Johnny. Tell me that isn't you.

93
00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:05.850
Huh?! Who's sayin' my name like they
think they know me or somethin'?!

94
00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:07.810
[gasps] Big Bro Zoro!

95
00:04:07.810 --> 00:04:09.310
[ZORO] Johnny! It is you.

96
00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.610
[JOHNNY] What are you doin' here, big bro?

97
00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:14.190
Hey, relax! Is everything
okay? Where's Yosaku?

98
00:04:14.190 --> 00:04:14.940
[JOHNNY] Well...

99
00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.860
[inaudible]

100
00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:20.410
Hey, look. Zoro knows that guy.

101
00:04:20.410 --> 00:04:21.990
What's going on here?

102
00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:29.870
[cries] He's been sick.

103
00:04:32.920 --> 00:04:34.880
[ZORO] What is it?

104
00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:36.090
[YOSAKU panting]

105
00:04:36.090 --> 00:04:39.430
[JOHNNY] Up until a few days ago,
he was healthy and full of life.

106
00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:40.380
And now...

107
00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:43.470
He keeps fainting!
And getting really pale!

108
00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:46.600
I have no idea what's causing it!

109
00:04:47.770 --> 00:04:52.270
[JOHNNY] His teeth have been falling out, and
his old wound opened up and started bleeding!

110
00:04:52.270 --> 00:04:55.860
He just got worse and worse! I
didn't know what to do!

111
00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.110
So I thought...

112
00:04:57.110 --> 00:05:00.530
Maybe we'd just rest on a
little island. But, then...

113
00:05:07.700 --> 00:05:11.670
[JOHNNY] A cannonball came
flying from this ship!

114
00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:18.010
[LUFFY, USOPP whimpering]

115
00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:23.340
[LUFFY, USOPP] We're very sorry!

116
00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.850
[JOHNNY] Sorry isn't good enough.

117
00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:28.720
[LUFFY, USOPP gasping]

118
00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:30.020
[YOSAKU panting]

119
00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.140
[JOHNNY] Isn't that right...

120
00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:33.480
partner!

121
00:05:35.190 --> 00:05:40.610
[JOHNNY] Big Bro. Give it to
me straight. Is he gonna die?!

122
00:05:40.610 --> 00:05:42.320
[ZORO gasps]

123
00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:45.580
[NAMI] So dumb.

124
00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.290
Watch it!

125
00:05:52.080 --> 00:05:55.250
Stop it! Whatever you're doing, stop!

126
00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:58.750
You're mocking his death!
Dammit! You'll...

127
00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.260
[NAMI] Luffy! Usopp! We have
some limes in storage.

128
00:06:02.260 --> 00:06:04.970
What're you doing?!
Bring them here! Now.

129
00:06:04.970 --> 00:06:05.680
[USOPP, LUFFY gasp]

130
00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:08.260
[USOPP, LUFFY arguing]

131
00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:21.030
He's got scurvy.

132
00:06:21.030 --> 00:06:22.110
[JOHNNY] Scurvy?

133
00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:25.820
[NAMI] Mm-hm. If we weren't too late,
he'll be just fine in a few days.

134
00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.280
[JOHNNY gasps]
Really, Big Sis?! Really?!

135
00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:30.910
Thank you, Big Sis!

136
00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:34.120
Please. Don't call me that.
It sounds so dumb.

137
00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.080
Besides, I'm not a magician.

138
00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.590
This used to be a hopeless
disease that plagued sailors,

139
00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.420
and we just know how
to deal with it now.

140
00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.670
– [LUFFY] Here,
– [USOPP] There you go,

141
00:06:41.670 --> 00:06:43.760
– drink up sick guy.
– have some more.

142
00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:48.430
[NAMI] This is caused by a simple deficiency
of plant-derived nutrients like Vitamin C.

143
00:06:48.430 --> 00:06:50.640
Back in the old days, they couldn't
carry fresh fruits and vegetables

144
00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:53.890
because they couldn't store
them. We know better now.

145
00:06:53.890 --> 00:06:56.440
[LUFFY] If a little is good,
a lot is gooder.

146
00:06:56.440 --> 00:06:58.020
[USOPP] You're gonna be just fine.

147
00:06:58.020 --> 00:06:59.770
[LUFFY] You're smart!

148
00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.820
You're like... a doctor!

149
00:07:01.820 --> 00:07:04.150
Well, now. How 'bout that.

150
00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:06.990
– I was right. She isn't dumb.
– [YOSAKU groaning]

151
00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:11.490
You guys, are morons. Every
sailor should know about scurvy!

152
00:07:12.750 --> 00:07:13.450
[YOSAKU coughs]

153
00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:16.420
[USOPP, LUFFY] Huh?

154
00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:15.580
[YOSAKU grunts]

155
00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:16.460
[NAMI gasps]

156
00:07:16.420 --> 00:07:18.210
[JOHNNY, YOSAKU] Hooray!
Hooray! Hooray! Hooray!

157
00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:19.750
Hooray! Hooray!

158
00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:20.630
[YOSAKU] cured me!

159
00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.550
[JOHNNY] Now you're all better!

160
00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:25.510
You can't heal that quickly!

161
00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:30.890
[JOHNNY, YOSAKU] Allow us
to introduce ourselves!

162
00:07:30.890 --> 00:07:33.270
My name is Johnny.

163
00:07:33.270 --> 00:07:34.980
And I'm Yosaku.

164
00:07:34.980 --> 00:07:39.860
<b>Johnny and Yosaku
Bounty Hunter Duo</b>

165
00:07:35.270 --> 00:07:39.860
Together, we're the baddest pirate
bounty hunting duo in the world.

166
00:07:39.860 --> 00:07:42.530
[JOHNNY] Big Bro Zoro
there used to be one of us.

167
00:07:42.530 --> 00:07:44.650
[YOSAKU] Glad to make your acquaintance.

168
00:07:46.030 --> 00:07:49.950
Small world. I never thought
I'd see you guys again.

169
00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:52.280
[JOHNNY] Well, if you
think you're surprised...

170
00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:57.210
[YOSAKU] We never imagined that the pirate
hunter Zoro became a pirate himself.

171
00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:59.040
[ZORO] Tell me about it.

172
00:07:59.040 --> 00:08:00.540
[JOHNNY] Big Bro.

173
00:08:00.540 --> 00:08:02.420
[YOSAKU] Ah!

174
00:08:02.420 --> 00:08:04.210
[YOSAKU groaning]

175
00:08:04.210 --> 00:08:06.260
[ZORO] Huh?

176
00:08:06.260 --> 00:08:08.340
Uh... Hey... Partner?!

177
00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.260
[YOSAKU groaning]

178
00:08:17.520 --> 00:08:19.230
[NAMI] Let this be a lesson to you.

179
00:08:19.730 --> 00:08:24.070
[ZORO] Yeah. This is the kind of trouble you
run into when you choose a life on the sea.

180
00:08:24.070 --> 00:08:27.530
[USOPP] Which means, when we're at sea,
we really gotta think about how we can get

181
00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:30.360
the right amount of nutrients
with very little food.

182
00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:34.410
It's absolutely necessary that someone
on this ship knows how to do that.

183
00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:39.040
[LUFFY] It's necessary?

184
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:41.830
Right! The ship needs a cook!

185
00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:42.590
[NAMI, USOPP] Hm?

186
00:08:42.590 --> 00:08:45.130
[LUFFY] Let's go find us a cook!

187
00:08:45.130 --> 00:08:47.050
I'm in! Good idea!

188
00:08:47.050 --> 00:08:49.590
We'll have yummy food,
even while we're out at sea!

189
00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:52.550
That's right. You got it. Ha, ha!

190
00:08:52.550 --> 00:08:54.890
A cook? I know just the place.

191
00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:57.640
And the food is gonna blow your mind.

192
00:08:57.640 --> 00:08:59.940
[JOHNNY] Consider yourselves warned.

193
00:08:59.940 --> 00:09:02.400
This place is close to the Grand Line.

194
00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:04.860
And I've heard a lot of rumors lately,

195
00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:08.690
that a certain hawk-eyed man
you're looking for is there.

196
00:09:10.360 --> 00:09:12.410
Set a course.

197
00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:14.330
North-Northeast!

198
00:09:14.330 --> 00:09:15.410
[NAMI] Yes!

199
00:09:15.410 --> 00:09:16.660
[USOPP] Awesome!

200
00:09:16.660 --> 00:09:17.580
[ZORO grunts]

201
00:09:17.580 --> 00:09:18.790
[LUFFY chuckles]

202
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.340
[JOHNNY] Our destination is...

203
00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:37.560
[JOHNNY] ... the sea restaurant...

204
00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:40.640
Baratie!

205
00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:42.310
<b>Baratie
The Sea Restaurant</b>

206
00:09:42.440 --> 00:09:43.940
[LUFFY, NAMI, USOPP] Ooooh!

207
00:09:43.940 --> 00:09:47.570
So, heh, what do you think?!

208
00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:49.820
[LUFFY] Wow. It's a big fish!

209
00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:50.740
[NAMI] How lovely!

210
00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:52.780
[USOPP] This is the coolest place ever!

211
00:09:52.780 --> 00:09:53.610
[LUFFY, USOPP cheer]

212
00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.080
[JOHNNY] Just like I told ya, right?!

213
00:09:56.080 --> 00:09:59.910
[horn blares, bell rings]

214
00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.210
Ah! What the...?!

215
00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.670
A Marine ship?!

216
00:10:04.670 --> 00:10:07.380
All the way out here?

217
00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:13.260
Hey, Luffy. They're not gonna
start firing at us, are they?

218
00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.850
But. How did that ship...?

219
00:10:18.970 --> 00:10:22.310
[FULLBODY] I've never
seen that pirate flag.

220
00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:26.310
So, do you think he knows that you
and I aren't a couple of pirates?

221
00:10:26.310 --> 00:10:27.230
[YOSAKU] Ah...

222
00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:34.530
<b>Lieutenant "Ironfist" Fullbody
Marine Headquarters</b>

223
00:10:29.360 --> 00:10:32.110
[FULLBODY] I am Iron Fist Fullbody!

224
00:10:32.110 --> 00:10:34.530
But, you can just call me "Sir"!

225
00:10:34.530 --> 00:10:38.280
You there! Who's the
captain?! Identify yourself!

226
00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.540
My name is Luffy!

227
00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:43.120
My name is Usopp. Got it?!

228
00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:46.580
We only made our flag
the day before yesterday!

229
00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:49.590
That's right marine! And I drew it!

230
00:10:50.340 --> 00:10:53.720
Heh. You did? Is that so...?

231
00:10:56.390 --> 00:10:59.600
Hey! You two! Right there!
I've seen you before.

232
00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:03.350
You're that bounty hunter duo that
goes after the small fish, right?

233
00:11:03.350 --> 00:11:04.690
Uh, well, we...

234
00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:07.770
[FULLBODY] So, you've finally
been caught by pirates.

235
00:11:07.770 --> 00:11:10.440
Uh. Well... Actually we...

236
00:11:10.440 --> 00:11:13.070
[FULLBODY laughs]
Now that's a laugh.

237
00:11:13.070 --> 00:11:15.240
Hey, c'mon baby, let's get going.

238
00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:15.780
Sure.

239
00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:17.570
[JOHNNY] Hey! Wait a minute!

240
00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:21.790
You think small time bounty
hunters would go after these guys?!

241
00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:28.460
Now. Let's go to that restaurant.

242
00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:31.710
[FULLBODY] They're an eyesore. Sink 'em.

243
00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.210
[BOTH] Sir!

244
00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.090
[JOHNNY] He ignored us!

245
00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:42.430
Next time we see him, he'd better
have a little more respect for us.

246
00:11:42.430 --> 00:11:44.850
[NAMI] Hm. What are these things?

247
00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:50.650
Well, those are all wanted
pirates, Big Sis Nam... Uh!

248
00:11:50.650 --> 00:11:51.650
[JOHNNY coughs]

249
00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:55.610
In other words, if we defeat
them, we get the reward money.

250
00:11:55.610 --> 00:11:59.160
Pretty lucrative business,
huh, Big Sis...?

251
00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:01.080
[NAMI grunting]

252
00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:09.040
Hey, you guys, look! They're
pointing a cannon right at us!

253
00:12:13.840 --> 00:12:15.130
Leave it to me!

254
00:12:15.130 --> 00:12:18.180
Now Gum-Gum...!

255
00:12:20.090 --> 00:12:21.180
[ALL groaning]

256
00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:22.850
[LUFFY] ... Slingshot!

257
00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.880
[COOK A] Sir!

258
00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:54.630
[COOK B] Are you all right,
Head Chef Zeff?!

259
00:12:54.630 --> 00:12:56.550
[COOK C] Sir, are you okay?!

260
00:13:00.050 --> 00:13:01.680
[COOK D] Head Chef,
are you sure you're okay?

261
00:13:01.680 --> 00:13:03.720
[ZEFF] No! Nothing is "okay"!

262
00:13:03.720 --> 00:13:05.350
[COOKS whimper]

263
00:13:06.060 --> 00:13:09.440
[ZEFF] Never mind, just get back
to the restaurant already!

264
00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:12.310
But... but, sir! Aren't you, I mean...

265
00:13:12.310 --> 00:13:14.650
[ZEFF] You maggots!
Do you want to see me angry?!

266
00:13:14.650 --> 00:13:16.110
[COOKS whimper]

267
00:13:16.110 --> 00:13:19.280
[ZEFF] Feeding the customer
is a cook's job!

268
00:13:19.280 --> 00:13:24.620
What are you trying to do?
Put me out of business?!

269
00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:29.790
[COOK C] This is the guy!

270
00:13:30.500 --> 00:13:33.500
[COOK D] He's the one
responsible for this!

271
00:13:33.500 --> 00:13:34.790
[ZEFF] Hm?

272
00:13:35.500 --> 00:13:38.460
[LUFFY] Sir, I'm very sorry!

273
00:13:38.460 --> 00:13:42.090
[LUFFY gasps]

274
00:13:42.090 --> 00:13:43.800
[screams] Your leg!

275
00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:44.510
[ZEFF] Idiot!

276
00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:47.640
Oh. I see. Good to know.

277
00:13:47.640 --> 00:13:49.310
[LUFFY groans]

278
00:13:51.270 --> 00:13:55.520
<b>Head Chef & Proprietor Zeff
Sea Restaurant</b>

279
00:13:52.350 --> 00:13:55.940
But... I'm all banged up...

280
00:13:55.940 --> 00:14:00.190
The medical fees and repair charges
for the ship are gonna cost you.

281
00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.240
[LUFFY grunts]

282
00:14:01.240 --> 00:14:02.530
[ZEFF sighs]

283
00:14:02.530 --> 00:14:04.620
[LUFFY] I won't ask you
to cut me any slack.

284
00:14:04.620 --> 00:14:06.830
Oh?

285
00:14:07.330 --> 00:14:08.080
[LUFFY] But...

286
00:14:08.080 --> 00:14:09.040
I'm flat broke!

287
00:14:09.040 --> 00:14:10.830
[ZEFF] Mm.

288
00:14:10.830 --> 00:14:13.710
Well, you're pretty direct, huh?

289
00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:18.050
If you don't have money,
you've no choice but to work.

290
00:14:18.050 --> 00:14:19.880
Fine. I wanna make it right!

291
00:14:19.880 --> 00:14:22.720
Then you'll work, unpaid,
for a whole year.

292
00:14:22.720 --> 00:14:24.970
[ZEFF] I'll let you
off the hook with that.

293
00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:27.430
Uh! A year?!

294
00:14:27.430 --> 00:14:30.720
Did you just say a year?!
A whole year?!

295
00:14:40.230 --> 00:14:42.320
[USOPP sighs] What's taking Luffy so long?

296
00:14:42.320 --> 00:14:43.650
[NAMI] Yeah...

297
00:14:43.650 --> 00:14:47.620
[USOPP] They'll probably make
him work without pay for like a whole month.

298
00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:50.040
[NAMI] He should've just said
it was the Marine's fault

299
00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.080
instead of being so freakin' honest.

300
00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:12.770
Oh wow. That guy sitting over
there is Lieutenant Fullbody.

301
00:15:12.770 --> 00:15:14.440
Well, what do you know.

302
00:15:14.440 --> 00:15:16.650
Hey, look kids. A big shot from HQ.

303
00:15:17.400 --> 00:15:19.940
Oh wow... He's so elegant.

304
00:15:19.940 --> 00:15:23.570
You're famous. Everybody
in here is looking at you.

305
00:15:23.570 --> 00:15:26.450
No, you're wrong.
They're all admiring you.

306
00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:32.040
[FULLBODY] Mm.

307
00:15:32.040 --> 00:15:34.750
So good!

308
00:15:34.750 --> 00:15:38.040
This... flavor...

309
00:15:38.040 --> 00:15:40.210
And yes... the aroma...

310
00:15:40.210 --> 00:15:43.920
It is the unmistakable scent from
the soil of Micquo of the North Land.

311
00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:47.300
Bitter with plenty of body,
and just a tad sour.

312
00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:50.140
This wine... must be...

313
00:15:50.140 --> 00:15:53.770
the famous Iturutz Burger Stein.

314
00:15:53.770 --> 00:15:57.480
Tell me waiter, am I right?!

315
00:15:57.480 --> 00:16:00.860
Uh-uh. Not even close, sir.

316
00:16:00.860 --> 00:16:02.190
[FULLBODY gasps]

317
00:16:03.320 --> 00:16:07.030
Eat up. This dish is best when hot.

318
00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:09.910
[FULLBODY] Uh.

319
00:16:11.120 --> 00:16:14.500
And, sir. My name's Sanji,
I'm the Sous Chef.

320
00:16:11.240 --> 00:16:15.620
<b>Sous-Chef Sanji
Sea Restaurant</b>

321
00:16:14.500 --> 00:16:17.750
All the waiters ran
off as of yesterday.

322
00:16:19.420 --> 00:16:21.460
[WOMAN laughs]

323
00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:25.460
[patrons laughing]

324
00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:26.970
[MAN A] You really shouldn't laugh.

325
00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:29.890
[WOMAN A] I can't help it!
He looked so confident!

326
00:16:31.350 --> 00:16:33.100
Do you know a lot?

327
00:16:33.100 --> 00:16:34.140
[FULLBODY gasps]

328
00:16:34.140 --> 00:16:35.220
About wine?

329
00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:37.480
Well, yes... I thought...

330
00:16:37.480 --> 00:16:40.150
But it seems my sense of
taste isn't working today.

331
00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:41.860
[WOMAN laughs]

332
00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:44.150
[FULLBODY] What's going on?!

333
00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:46.990
I'm certain I requested that the owner
serve that particular wine

334
00:16:46.990 --> 00:16:48.820
when I made this reservation!

335
00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:55.160
I can only work... for one week!

336
00:16:55.160 --> 00:16:58.580
Yeah. Right. A week, get real!

337
00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:00.000
Fine then. Two!

338
00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:01.580
Hey! You wrecked my restaurant

339
00:17:01.580 --> 00:17:04.960
and seriously injured the Head
Chef. That's a serious offense!

340
00:17:04.960 --> 00:17:08.420
You can't just settle that up with
one or two weeks of unpaid work!

341
00:17:08.420 --> 00:17:09.630
That's ridiculous!

342
00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:13.010
[LUFFY] You win! Three weeks!

343
00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:17.810
Talk to me... with respect!

344
00:17:17.810 --> 00:17:18.930
– [ZEFF yells]
– [LUFFY gasps]

345
00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:26.570
[ZEFF grunts]

346
00:17:27.780 --> 00:17:28.940
[LUFFY] No deal.

347
00:17:28.940 --> 00:17:29.950
[ZEFF] Hm?

348
00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:34.280
I waited ten long years
to become a pirate. So...

349
00:17:34.280 --> 00:17:38.080
I'm not gonna waste another
year stuck in this restaurant!

350
00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:39.370
[ZEFF] Mm?

351
00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:40.620
'Kay. Listen.

352
00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:43.290
I'm gonna get you to let
me off the hook in a week.

353
00:17:43.290 --> 00:17:45.630
That's my decision!

354
00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:48.340
If you value your time so much,

355
00:17:48.340 --> 00:17:51.470
I'll tell you what you can do
to settle your debt quickly.

356
00:17:51.470 --> 00:17:52.550
Ya runt!

357
00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:54.600
[LUFFY groans]

358
00:17:54.600 --> 00:17:58.970
It'll cost you... a leg, my boy.

359
00:17:58.970 --> 00:17:59.980
[LUFFY grunts]

360
00:17:59.980 --> 00:18:01.730
That's pricey.

361
00:18:01.730 --> 00:18:04.770
Heh. Good, I got your attention.

362
00:18:14.910 --> 00:18:17.030
Waiter! Hey! Get over here!

363
00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:18.410
[SANJI] Hm.

364
00:18:20.160 --> 00:18:26.210
[SANJI] I believe I've already
told you, I'm not a waiter.

365
00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:30.840
What an irresistible beauty you are.

366
00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:31.920
My lady.

367
00:18:31.920 --> 00:18:34.970
Would you care to join me
elsewhere for a glass of wine?

368
00:18:35.800 --> 00:18:36.680
[SANJI] Hm?

369
00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:37.850
Hey! What is this?!

370
00:18:37.850 --> 00:18:41.430
Is "bug soup" on the menu today,
or did you make it just for me?

371
00:18:41.430 --> 00:18:42.680
Bug soup?

372
00:18:42.680 --> 00:18:47.310
That's right. What's this
bug doing there, waiter?

373
00:18:47.310 --> 00:18:50.480
[FULLBODY] This is gonna ruin
their restaurant's reputation.

374
00:18:50.480 --> 00:18:53.900
Sorry, sir. Don't know, really.
Looks like he's floating.

375
00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:54.910
[FULLBODY grunts]

376
00:18:54.910 --> 00:18:57.030
Then again. It kinda
looks like he's drowning.

377
00:18:57.030 --> 00:18:59.080
But it's hard to say for sure.

378
00:18:59.080 --> 00:18:59.910
[WOMAN laughs]

379
00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.700
[patrons laughing]

380
00:19:02.700 --> 00:19:05.750
[FULLBODY seething]

381
00:19:10.630 --> 00:19:14.800
Don't you mess with me! Waiter!

382
00:19:24.270 --> 00:19:27.770
[SANJI] You could've eaten it if
you had just taken the bug out.

383
00:19:27.770 --> 00:19:29.690
It would've been wonderful.

384
00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:32.230
It took three full days of hard cooking

385
00:19:32.230 --> 00:19:36.110
to prepare that soup for
you, and you wasted it.

386
00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:40.490
[FULLBODY] Can't you see that you're
biting off more than you can chew?

387
00:19:43.040 --> 00:19:45.830
I'm the customer here!
Do you understand me?!

388
00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:46.960
I'm paying you!

389
00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:48.580
Stop it! Fullbody!

390
00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:49.630
Shut up!

391
00:19:49.630 --> 00:19:51.000
[WOMAN gasps]

392
00:19:51.000 --> 00:19:53.880
No... Fullbody... No...

393
00:19:53.880 --> 00:19:58.220
Can your money truly
satisfy your hunger?

394
00:19:58.220 --> 00:19:59.510
Whadya mean?

395
00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:05.850
[SANJI] I'm asking...
Can it satisfy your hunger?

396
00:20:05.850 --> 00:20:06.730
[LUFFY] No!

397
00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:09.310
No! No!

398
00:20:10.810 --> 00:20:12.270
This is getting old.

399
00:20:12.270 --> 00:20:15.740
You're never gonna make it if
you don't just give in sometimes!

400
00:20:15.740 --> 00:20:20.450
[panting] It's still no!

401
00:20:20.450 --> 00:20:22.910
[growls] No respect!

402
00:20:29.420 --> 00:20:32.250
[patrons whimpering]

403
00:20:34.130 --> 00:20:36.170
[WOMAN] Fullbody?

404
00:20:36.170 --> 00:20:37.630
It... It's Sanji.

405
00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:40.300
What's going on here?

406
00:20:40.300 --> 00:20:41.260
[ZORO] Hm.

407
00:20:41.260 --> 00:20:42.850
A fight...

408
00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:52.360
[FULLBODY groaning]

409
00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:56.190
Don't ever waste food around me again.

410
00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:59.360
[FULLBODY choking]

411
00:20:59.360 --> 00:21:01.870
At sea, if you ever provoke your cook,

412
00:21:01.870 --> 00:21:05.700
you're signing your own
death warrant. Remember that.

413
00:21:14.960 --> 00:21:16.880
[MAN A] Just hold it... almost there...

414
00:21:16.880 --> 00:21:19.170
[PATTY] Customer service equals love!

415
00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:21.590
And love equals restaurant!

416
00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:22.970
[PATTY] The customer...

417
00:21:22.970 --> 00:21:25.140
... is the king! [screams]

418
00:21:25.140 --> 00:21:28.100
Pleasant greetings to the
customer is what it's all about,

419
00:21:28.100 --> 00:21:31.100
the customer is always right,
and we stand by that!

420
00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:34.980
<b>Cook Patty
Sea Restaurant</b>

421
00:21:31.100 --> 00:21:33.400
Hello and welcome, you damn crooks...

422
00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:35.110
But don't you ever come back!

423
00:21:35.110 --> 00:21:37.030
Awfully sorry about that...

424
00:21:37.030 --> 00:21:40.360
You're all so pathetic, I laugh!

425
00:21:40.360 --> 00:21:42.160
[laughs]

426
00:21:42.160 --> 00:21:42.780
[PATTY] Done!

427
00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:43.990
– [PATTY] Ah! Yes, indeed!
– [MAN A gasps]

428
00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:47.160
Today will be a great day for everyone!

429
00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:49.330
Oh, hello there and
welcome, you damn crook.

430
00:21:49.330 --> 00:21:54.880
That's our service motto around here,
no doubt about it, the customer is... Ah! Huh?

431
00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:57.000
[PATTY] Oh, no! Our customer!

432
00:21:57.000 --> 00:21:59.260
Dammit! Not again, Sanji!

433
00:21:59.260 --> 00:22:01.590
What do you think you're
doing to our customer?!

434
00:22:01.590 --> 00:22:04.340
Can't you see he's
a Marine Lieutenant?!

435
00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:06.560
You're a terrible cook.

436
00:22:06.560 --> 00:22:09.310
What makes you think that
you can talk to me like that?

437
00:22:09.310 --> 00:22:13.060
[PATTY grunts] A crappy cook
like you is calling me bad?

438
00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:15.900
Restaurants can't exist
without their customers!

439
00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:20.110
They're our lifeblood, so we don't want
to hurt them the way you seem to keep doing!

440
00:22:20.110 --> 00:22:22.150
But he deserved it.

441
00:22:22.150 --> 00:22:27.490
He didn't treat the food or me with
respect... and he insulted all the cooks.

442
00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:32.210
– [FULLBODY grunts]
– [SANJI] So I simply

443
00:22:32.210 --> 00:22:33.870
taught him a lesson.

444
00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:38.550
[FULLBODY grunts]
You're gonna to regret this...

445
00:22:38.550 --> 00:22:40.010
All of you...

446
00:22:40.010 --> 00:22:43.010
No restaurant should treat
its customers like this...

447
00:22:43.010 --> 00:22:45.890
I'll shut you down...
Do you understand me?!

448
00:22:45.890 --> 00:22:48.970
I will shut you down!
This entire place!

449
00:22:49.510 --> 00:22:52.100
This whole restaurant is
finished! Do you hear me?!

450
00:22:52.100 --> 00:22:55.770
Then, maybe I should
just finish you off now.

451
00:22:56.520 --> 00:22:57.730
[FULLBODY gasps]

452
00:22:57.730 --> 00:22:59.110
[COOK LI] Sous Chef Sanji, stop it!

453
00:22:59.110 --> 00:23:00.780
– [COOK LI yelling]
– Arrogant assholes like you

454
00:23:00.780 --> 00:23:04.700
who think they're such big shots they can
push anybody around really piss me off!

455
00:23:04.700 --> 00:23:07.200
You can't keep doing this in
the restaurant every other day!

456
00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:08.330
[SANJI growls]

457
00:23:08.330 --> 00:23:11.200
You're not such a big
shot now, are ya? Are ya?!

458
00:23:11.200 --> 00:23:13.500
[FULLBODY growling]

459
00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:15.120
[ZEFF, LUFFY grunt]

460
00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:18.540
[customers gasping]

461
00:23:18.540 --> 00:23:20.090
[USOPP sighs]

462
00:23:20.090 --> 00:23:22.920
– [CUSTOMER A] What happened?
– [CUSTOMER B] Are they okay?

463
00:23:22.920 --> 00:23:23.880
[ZEFF growls]

464
00:23:23.880 --> 00:23:25.630
[LUFFY gasps]
I can breathe again!

465
00:23:25.630 --> 00:23:27.010
Boss Zeff, what's happening here?

466
00:23:27.010 --> 00:23:28.600
You didn't hurt yourself, did you?

467
00:23:28.600 --> 00:23:29.760
Dammit!

468
00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:30.930
My ceiling!

469
00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:33.600
Another thing that's gonna have
to get fixed because of you!

470
00:23:33.600 --> 00:23:35.600
This is all your fault, you brat!

471
00:23:35.600 --> 00:23:37.560
How is it my fault?! You attacked me!

472
00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:40.650
Boss, can you stop messing
around and give us a hand?

473
00:23:40.650 --> 00:23:42.650
Sanji's gone crazy again!

474
00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:43.690
[COOKS, SANJI growling]

475
00:23:43.690 --> 00:23:46.070
– [ZEFF] Hey, Sanji!
– [SANJI growling]

476
00:23:46.070 --> 00:23:49.620
[ZEFF] Don't tell me you went
on another rampage in here, you idiot!

477
00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:50.910
Put a cork in it, old man!

478
00:23:50.910 --> 00:23:53.080
[ZEFF] Oh, now you're ordering me around!

479
00:23:53.700 --> 00:23:55.660
Just who do you think
you're talking to?!

480
00:23:55.660 --> 00:23:58.500
Do you want to sink my restaurant
to the bottom of the sea?!

481
00:23:58.500 --> 00:24:00.790
You punk!

482
00:24:00.790 --> 00:24:02.500
– [FULLBODY laughs]
– [ZEFF] You, too!

483
00:24:02.500 --> 00:24:04.260
Get your ass out of my restaurant!

484
00:24:04.260 --> 00:24:07.430
[FULLBODY groans, grunts]

485
00:24:07.430 --> 00:24:10.100
[FULLBODY groans]

486
00:24:10.100 --> 00:24:12.810
[FULLBODY] What kind
of restaurant is this?!

487
00:24:12.810 --> 00:24:14.810
That boss is like a gangster.

488
00:24:14.810 --> 00:24:19.230
It's almost as if... if...
this were a pirate ship!

489
00:24:19.230 --> 00:24:21.980
How can you deny our motto
that the customer is king?!

490
00:24:21.980 --> 00:24:25.610
The only kingly customers are the ones
who stomach the slop that you call food.

491
00:24:25.610 --> 00:24:26.990
That's it. If you two wanna fight,

492
00:24:27.530 --> 00:24:30.030
you'll keep it in the
kitchen, you understand me?!

493
00:24:30.030 --> 00:24:33.330
[FULLBODY grunts]
Are all these idiots really cooks?

494
00:24:33.330 --> 00:24:35.370
[MARINE B] Lieu... Lieutenant!

495
00:24:35.370 --> 00:24:36.870
Lieutenant Fullbody!

496
00:24:36.870 --> 00:24:37.960
[FULLBODY gasps]

497
00:24:37.960 --> 00:24:41.460
[MARINE B panting]
We've... We've got trouble!

498
00:24:41.460 --> 00:24:43.630
Wow, this restaurant is crazy.

499
00:24:43.630 --> 00:24:44.960
Sir, he's escaped!

500
00:24:44.960 --> 00:24:47.590
Pirate Krieg's henchman
attacked us and vanished!

501
00:24:47.590 --> 00:24:48.590
He what?!

502
00:24:48.590 --> 00:24:51.590
Well, sir, we've already lost seven of our men,
and the only thing we wanted

503
00:24:51.590 --> 00:24:53.720
out of him was a lead
on finding Krieg...

504
00:24:53.720 --> 00:24:54.680
Impossible...

505
00:24:54.680 --> 00:24:56.350
When we picked him up three days ago,

506
00:24:56.350 --> 00:24:58.440
he was right on the verge
of starving to death.

507
00:24:58.440 --> 00:25:01.270
And we haven't fed him anything.
Where'd he get the strength?

508
00:25:01.270 --> 00:25:02.400
Krieg Pirates?

509
00:25:02.400 --> 00:25:03.570
[customers murmuring]

510
00:25:03.570 --> 00:25:07.150
[CUSTOMER D] They're the ones who're said
to be the fiercest pirates in the East Blue!

511
00:25:07.150 --> 00:25:08.190
I'm sorry, Lieutenant, I...

512
00:25:08.190 --> 00:25:10.160
[gunshot]

513
00:25:10.160 --> 00:25:12.820
[customers gasp]

514
00:25:12.820 --> 00:25:15.040
[footsteps]

515
00:25:15.040 --> 00:25:16.040
[ZEFF grunts]

516
00:25:16.040 --> 00:25:17.040
[SANJI] Huh?

517
00:25:17.040 --> 00:25:18.040
[LUFFY gasps]

518
00:25:21.330 --> 00:25:23.670
It would seem we have
a new customer, sir.

519
00:25:23.670 --> 00:25:28.380
He'd do well to mind his manners and
not start any trouble on my ship.

520
00:25:28.380 --> 00:25:29.840
A pirate, huh?

521
00:25:32.390 --> 00:25:33.390
[FULLBODY grunts]

522
00:25:43.020 --> 00:25:46.400
I don't care what it is...
Just bring me something to eat.

523
00:25:48.610 --> 00:25:50.780
Come on... This is a restaurant.

524
00:25:50.780 --> 00:25:53.030
Hello and welcome, you damn crook!

525
00:25:53.030 --> 00:25:54.490
[customers gasp]

526
00:25:54.490 --> 00:25:56.490
I'm just gonna say this one more time.

527
00:25:56.490 --> 00:25:59.040
Bring me something to
eat and make it quick.

528
00:25:59.040 --> 00:26:00.910
That cook is gonna get us killed.

529
00:26:00.910 --> 00:26:03.080
Of course, right away,
but might I be so bold

530
00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:05.540
to inquire how you're
paying for your meal?

531
00:26:09.050 --> 00:26:10.380
Will a bullet be enough?

532
00:26:10.380 --> 00:26:12.220
So you don't have any money then.

533
00:26:13.090 --> 00:26:14.220
– [FULLBODY] What?
– [customers gasp]

534
00:26:14.220 --> 00:26:16.470
That dumb ass, Patty,
broke another chair.

535
00:26:16.470 --> 00:26:18.060
Whoa... What power...

536
00:26:19.850 --> 00:26:23.140
Sorry, pirate, but our policy is
to only serve paying customers.

537
00:26:23.140 --> 00:26:24.150
– [customers whistle, cheer]
– You tell him!

538
00:26:24.150 --> 00:26:25.110
Kick his ass, Patty.

539
00:26:25.770 --> 00:26:28.190
Show that pirate we
cooks don't screw around!

540
00:26:28.190 --> 00:26:29.280
[stomach rumbles]

541
00:26:29.280 --> 00:26:33.400
[PATTY] Aww, I can hear
your stomach grumbling from here, pirate.

542
00:26:33.400 --> 00:26:35.490
That was a fart, jerk.

543
00:26:35.490 --> 00:26:36.280
Now, listen...

544
00:26:36.280 --> 00:26:38.950
Get me... something... to eat now...

545
00:26:38.950 --> 00:26:41.410
We're not getting you
anything, so beat it!

546
00:26:47.290 --> 00:26:49.170
[FULLBODY] I can't take anymore.

547
00:26:49.170 --> 00:26:51.510
All of these cooks are insane!

548
00:26:51.510 --> 00:26:53.170
I've gotta get outta here.

549
00:26:53.170 --> 00:26:55.590
I don't want anything to do
with this place ever again!

550
00:26:55.590 --> 00:27:00.140
[cheering continues]

551
00:27:00.140 --> 00:27:02.480
[PATTY] And now, you damn crooks...

552
00:27:02.480 --> 00:27:06.150
If you need anything,
just ask, okay? [laughs]

553
00:27:09.440 --> 00:27:11.440
And please, never come back.

554
00:27:11.990 --> 00:27:12.990
[PATTY grunts]

555
00:27:15.610 --> 00:27:16.740
[GHIN groans]
Dammit,

556
00:27:16.740 --> 00:27:20.580
if I wasn't so weak from hunger,
I'd be inside eating...

557
00:27:40.390 --> 00:27:42.890
[SANJI] It's amazing
how beautiful and cruel

558
00:27:42.890 --> 00:27:45.940
this ocean can be, how it's
almost a death sentence

559
00:27:45.940 --> 00:27:50.230
to lose your food and water out here,
how difficult it is to survive.

560
00:27:50.230 --> 00:27:52.400
I know what it means to go hungry

561
00:27:52.400 --> 00:27:55.070
because of the sea more than anyone.

562
00:27:55.070 --> 00:27:58.780
You can die for your pride if you want.

563
00:27:58.780 --> 00:28:02.080
But listen, if you and eat and survive,
won't that give you the opportunity

564
00:28:02.080 --> 00:28:05.410
